/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nX∨(X∧Y)≡X.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $X.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Y∧X)∨X & ≡X∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡X∨(X∧Y) \\\\  & ≡X.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∨(X∧Y) & ≡Y∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡Y≢X.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f510f76-f3c6-5a7a-b248-a17219184fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407292} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb016f2-03b4-57bf-9fcc-8b9cdc170a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407293} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c92d20-75ab-5758-8f5c-12c90997983b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407297} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b2ca85-080e-5af9-b237-63e3fefef845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407298} {:answer/id #uuid "f8be1cf7-b273-55bf-a561-7d5869642a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb016f2-03b4-57bf-9fcc-8b9cdc170a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407293} :answer-field/id #uuid "43de8a0c-6ffb-50fa-9e93-31fde48b6d17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9f0b645-6838-5cad-b5bd-0b7bf64c64fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-81276" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $C?$\n\n- $B∨(B∨C)$\n- $B∧(B∨C)$\n- $C∧(B∨C)$" :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nC∧(C∨B)≡C.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∧(B∨C) & ≡B≢C.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∧(B∨C) & ≡C∧(C∨B) \\\\  & ≡C.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1835dbe5-7a53-5bf2-a332-74cb2d5f68f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407287} {:answer/id #uuid "195e7fd9-c549-5aab-828f-eeabfcdeb266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407288} {:answer/id #uuid "303cbb99-bbc1-5f11-9171-09fabe0ff92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407290} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3655f9-81c0-5fdb-a48d-05082b26b7d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407291} {:answer/id #uuid "d09757aa-fd5d-54fd-b3d1-49c505fad041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09757aa-fd5d-54fd-b3d1-49c505fad041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407296} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef12586-e2eb-58c0-8a26-29cbae2f1aeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "669b0027-14f5-5068-b932-b9686df06625" :question/math-academy-id "q-81717" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $R?$\n\n- $(T∨R)∧T$\n- $R∧(T∨R)$\n- $(R∨T)∧R$" :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nR∧(R∨T)≡R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(T∨R)∧T & ≡T∧(T∨R) \\\\  & ≡T≢R.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R∧(T∨R) & ≡R∧(R∨T) \\\\  & ≡R.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(R∨T)∧R & ≡R∧(R∨T) \\\\  & ≡R.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
